  "id": "instrumentalism",
  "term": "instrumentalism",
  "definition": "In developmental psychology, instrumentalism refers to treating childhood mainly as a means to future adult outcomes rather than valuing the child’s present experience and agency. In this adult-centered view, development is framed as preparation for a later ideal instead of a reciprocal, current process of becoming.",
